Day 4 of 90 with @MyFirstHack, and today I looked inside my own laptop for the first time.
I always treated it like a magic box: open it, use it, close it. Today I opened Task Manager and saw 14 connections to servers around the world that I never knowingly started.
That was a strange feeling. It's my device, but I had no idea what it was doing in the background.
The exercise was to pick 3 processes I didn't recognise and Google them. The most surprising one was a background process I'd never heard of, constantly talking to a company I don't even use.
What stuck with me: cybersecurity people don't see computers as magic. They see systems they can understand and reason about.
86 days left, and the gap between "I use a computer" and "I understand a computer" is getting smaller. 💻
